course: dictionary
lesson: 4791
title: Meaning from context: humanist
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a hard word from the words around it. These are its context, and they leave clues. «Humanists use the Golden Rule as a reasoned basis for treating others well, without needing belief in God.» The clues are reasoned, treating others well and without belief in God, so a humanist is someone who is kind and thinks clearly without believing in God.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A humanist can be a person, or humanist can describe ideas. In «a humanist wedding», humanist is an adjective: it tells you what kind of wedding it is. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Try «Humanists believe meaning comes from how we live and love in this one life.» If your meaning makes sense there, you are probably right. If it does not, read the words around the word again.
fact: A humanist is a person who lives by reason, science and kindness, without needing religion.
fact: As an adjective, humanist describes ideas or ceremonies, like a humanist wedding or a humanist funeral, which have no prayers.
fact: In history, a humanist was a scholar of the Renaissance who studied the writings of ancient Greece and Rome.
fact: Humanists hold ceremonies such as weddings, baby namings and funerals.
fact: Humanists UK is an organisation that supports humanists.
exercise: «Humanists believe this life is the only one and that people can be good using reason and compassion.» What is a humanist? | A person who builds castles | *A person who lives by reason and kindness, without needing God | A person who has never been to school | A person who prays to many gods every day
exercise: «Humanists try to live good lives by reason and compassion.» What does compassion mean? | Running very fast | A loud noise | *Caring about other people's pain | Being very rich
exercise: «She had a humanist funeral, with no prayers.» What does humanist describe here? | A church with a tall bell tower | *The kind of funeral, which follows humanist ideas | A famous singer at the service | A flower shop by the sea
test: «In history, a humanist was a scholar of the Renaissance who studied the writings of ancient Greece and Rome.» What did a Renaissance humanist study? | Only the stars in the sky | Modern computer games | Maps of the ocean | *Old writings from ancient Greece and Rome
test: Humanist can be a noun or an adjective. In «He is a humanist who believes in reason», which is it? | *A noun, meaning a person | An adjective, describing a wedding | A verb, meaning to run | A noun, meaning a church leader
exam: Which words in «Humanists use the Golden Rule as a reasoned basis for treating others well, without needing belief in God.» show that a humanist does not need God? | reasoned basis | *without needing belief in God | treating others well | the Golden Rule
